ture to describe situations where the results are automatic or usual. You use the zero conditional to suggest why you are 100% sure of the result.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use both <span class=\"italic\">if</span> and <span class=\"italic\">when</span> with the zero conditional.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class =\\\"strong\\\">Condition</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Result</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">When the water freezes</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">the cracks in the rocks get bigger.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If it's bright</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">we wear our sunglasses.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If it's hot</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">we drink more water.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You have to book 6 months ahead if you want a permit.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When you want a permit, you book 6 months ahead.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If the tour has a cancellation, we can go into the canyon.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "lucky ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having good fortune ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We are so lucky we got a permit!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le14ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about a tour in the Grand Canyon.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "permit ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a document that says you can do something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You need a permit to go hiking in the Grand Canyon.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le14ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to set the alarm", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to decide when to have the clock wake you up", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Set the alarm for 5 a.m.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le14ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "gigantic ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "huge; enormous ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The canyon is gigantic.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le14ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "sea level", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the average height of the sea where it meets the land", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The canyon is a mile above sea level.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le14ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "canyon ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a deep valley with water at the bottom ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We visited the Grand Canyon last year.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le14ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "trail mix ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a mixture of nuts, seeds and dried fruit  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Let's take some trail mix to eat for energy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le14ob01aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "crack ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a narrow opening ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The rocks have cracks in them.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le14ob01aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "rocky", "type": "name"}, {"content": "covered with small stones ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Grand Canyon is rocky and dry.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le14ob01aud09", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Choose one of the Seven Natural Wonders you would like to see.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Do research and read about it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 5 to 7 sentences to describe it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your sentences to a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Listen to your partner's sentences.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I write about a Natural Wonder.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about geographical features.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my sentences aloud.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I listen to my partner read.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn4le14ob01re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn4le14ob01re2img05.jpg", "time": "1", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: We're so lucky we can go into the canyon! I'm glad there is a cancellation.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Usually you have to book 6 months ahead if you want a permit.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: We should be ready at 6 a.m. Let's fill our backpacks.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Good idea."}, {"image": "engenn4le14ob01re2img01.jpg", "time": "15000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: When should I set the alarm for?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I think 5 a.m. so that we can have breakfast.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: What about snacks?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Trail mix is good. </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: The canyon is gigantic!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: We're a mile above sea level!"}, {"image": "engenn4le14ob01re2img02.jpg", "time": "27400", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: It looks so rocky and dry. There are lots of rock formations!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yeah. When it freezes, the cracks in the rocks get bigger!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Amazing. Are we prepared?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yes. If it's bright, we wear our sunglasses!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Yeah. When it's hot, we drink more water.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yep! All ready!</br>"}], "audiosrc": "engenn4le14ob01re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn4le14ob01re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can ask for and respond to suggestions. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can give extended warnings, recommendations, or advice.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about geographical features.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Vocabulary and Grammar", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Do you know some tourist attractions that are na